#### Dead Code Injection
Dead code injection is an extremely common technique used by hackers who want to make their programs harder to reverse engineer or analyze. It can be done easily with any programming language since all you need to do is add some unreachable code into your project. Here is how dead code injection works:

![](https://cdn-images-1.medium.com/max/800/1*vPzR9TpVuXQYJZhOwBkAuw.png)

As you can see from the image above, there’s no way for the computer to reach line 10 but the compiler will still compile the entire method as if everything was fine. There are many ways to inject dead code such as adding comments or empty lines. Let’s examine our example below:

```java
public class Test{
	void foo(){
