This solution uses [Dijkstra's algorithm](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dijkstra%27s_algorithm). To implement Dijkstra's algorithm we need two things: A graph data structure and a way to compute distances between nodes. We can use arrays as graphs since they are mutable and have constant time access times. For computing distances we will use BFS which runs in O(V+E) where V is the total number of vertices and E is the total number of edges. Since there are only O(N^2) edges and N is bounded by the maximum possible width and height of the grid, our runtime complexity is O(N^2).

