In this case, auto refers to the type of variable v. Since v is already declared at that point, move will try to cast v to rvalue reference. However, since v is already an lvalue, moving it doesn’t change anything. Therefore, the statement is equivalent to declaring a non-reference variable v and assigning it the same value as the existing variable v.

